## 2026-09-07 placement, destruction and anti-soft-lock contract
Reuse current #1033/#1012, #2605 placement and #2600 rollback WIP. Shared placement/authority files serialize.

The player may choose defenses/Core position, but a valid match must retain declared access/counterplay. Revalidate placement against authoritative terrain/structure state, player/team rights, support/collision and the actual route policy. Handle a terrain change or another placement between preview and server commit; reject/rollback without double cost or stale invisible collision.

Test full blocking attempts, Core relocation during existing creep targeting, destruction during pending nav update, support removal and repeated undo/refund as applicable. Server gameplay health/collision determines access; Chaos debris presentation cannot keep an invisible permanent blocker or award duplicate damage/refund.

Show place -> defend -> enemy counter -> reopened route -> renewed Core pressure through normal controls on both clients. Keep free earthworks separate from construction economy. The final outcome belongs in #803/#941, not a standalone placement demo.

---

Parent: #803 / #941. Compose existing Core relocation plus #1033 construction and existing destruction; do not add another placement or objective system.

Acceptance:
- each player can choose a valid Core position in/around the live base through normal controls;
- the player can place existing walls/defences to make that position meaningfully easier to defend;
- the enemy can attack/destroy defences and reopen access rather than creating a permanent soft lock;
- invalid Core/defence placements fail visibly and preserve a playable route;
- both clients see the same authoritative Core/base state;
- prove the loop as player choice -> build defence -> enemy counterplay -> Core pressure.
